      "reason": "The flagged copy serves authorized media capabilities rather than panel HTML. It always rebuilds headers with a restrictive CSP sandbox, default-src none, nosniff and DENY; upstream CSP and cookies cannot relax the boundary. Resource paths reject active MIME types. Regression tests confirm opaque media bytes and restrictive headers remain intact, so escaping the media body would break supported content without fixing an established XSS.",
