    {
      "id": "fixed-loopback-healthcheck-tls",
      "ruleId": "go/disabled-certificate-check",
      "path": "cmd/meridian/command_line.go",
      "partialFingerprints": {
        "primaryLocationLineHash": "6d632b862fb273c2:1"
      },
      "reason": "The verification exception is restricted to the separate local healthcheck client, fixed 127.0.0.1 and ::1 targets, a range-validated panel-port marker and a constant unauthenticated path. Redirects are disabled, no credentials are sent, and upstream business clients retain certificate verification. Public-domain panel certificates do not normally name loopback, so this narrowly scoped liveness probe is an intentional exception.",
